From: Nerves ROCK Pi S maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: accept positive misc_read length

The RK3308 OTP misc driver returns the number of bytes read on success.
The generic Rockchip CPUID helpers incorrectly treat every non-zero return as
an error, causing misc_init_r() to return -1 and abort the initcall sequence.
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/misc.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/misc.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/misc.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/misc.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/misc.c
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@ int rockchip_cpuid_from_efuse(const u32 cpuid_offset,
 
 	/* read the cpu_id range from the efuses */
 	ret = misc_read(dev, cpuid_offset, cpuid, cpuid_length);
-	if (ret) {
+	if (ret < 0) {
 		debug("%s: reading cpuid from the efuses failed\n",
 		      __func__);
 		return -1;
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@ int rockchip_cpuid_from_otp(const u32 cpuid_offset,
 
 	/* read the cpu_id range from the otp */
 	ret = misc_read(dev, cpuid_offset, cpuid, cpuid_length);
-	if (ret) {
+	if (ret < 0) {
 		debug("%s: reading cpuid from the otp failed\n",
 		      __func__);
 		return -1;
-- 
2.43.0
